# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit the filled-in `.env`.
#
# Use `.env`, not `.env.local`: the Prisma CLI only reads `.env`, and Next.js
# reads it as well, so one file serves both. Supabase Dashboard ->
# Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string.
#
# 🔴 PERCENT-ENCODE SPECIAL CHARACTERS IN THE PASSWORD. This is not theoretical:
# it broke the app on 2026-08-19 during the Mumbai move, and the symptom lies.
#   &  ->  %26        $  ->  %24        @  ->  %40
#   #  ->  %23        ?  ->  %3F        /  ->  %2F        %  ->  %25 (first)
#
# A `$` makes dotenv perform VARIABLE EXPANSION before Prisma sees the string, so
# the app authenticates with a different password than the one in this file --
# while psql, `prisma migrate status` and any script that reads the file itself
# all connect perfectly. Errors seen: "Can't reach database server", then
# "Authentication failed ... credentials for `postgres` are not valid".
# See Gotcha 3d in CLAUDE.md.

# APP RUNTIME - Supavisor SESSION mode, port 5432.
#
# NOT the transaction pooler on :6543. Benchmarked 2026-08-19 on this project:
# the same trivial query took 1,175ms median through :6543 and 230ms through
# :5432 - the transaction pooler was adding ~950ms to EVERY query. `pgbouncer=true`
# is gone with it (it disables prepared statements, which session mode does not need).
#
# This is safe here because ONE person uses the app at a time. The transaction
# pooler exists so many concurrent serverless functions can share few Postgres
# connections; on a multi-user product this trade would be the wrong way round.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-1-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?connection_limit=5"

# DIRECT - Supavisor SESSION mode, port 5432. `prisma migrate` only.
# 🔴 USE THE POOLER HOST, never db.<project-ref>.supabase.co. That host failed to
# resolve from this network on 2026-08-12 AND again on 2026-08-19 with a fresh
# project ("could not translate host name"). It is IPv6-only without the paid
# IPv4 add-on.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-1-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# Random 32+ char string. Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=""

# http://localhost:3000 in dev, the production URL on Vercel.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
